import{_ as a,o as i,c as t,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const d=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 915 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 14 — The Cross-Plane Operation Reporting System","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 915 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 14 — The Cross-Plane Operation Reporting System","no":915,"module":5,"tags":["Charter","Article 14","Cross-Plane","Reporting System","Operation Norms"],"related":["81-Plane-Traversal Rules","88-Cross-Plane Ethics Guidelines","28-Cross-Plane Anchor Connection"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0915_模块5-第十四条-跨位面操作报备制.md","filePath":"en/0915_模块5-第十四条-跨位面操作报备制.md"}'),r={name:"en/0915_模块5-第十四条-跨位面操作报备制.md"};function o(s,e,l,c,p,u){return i(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-915-myriad-rank-republican-civilizational-charter-·-article-14-—-the-cross-plane-operation-reporting-system" tabindex="-1">Entry 915 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 14 — The Cross-Plane Operation Reporting System <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-915-myriad-rank-republican-civilizational-charter-·-article-14-—-the-cross-plane-operation-reporting-system" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 915 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 14 — The Cross-Plane Operation Reporting System&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 5 · Civilization Final-Finalization Canonical Entries | Benchmark base: Documents 81, 88, 28</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-every-cross-plane-trip-must-leave-a-name" tabindex="-1">Introduction: every cross-plane trip must leave a name <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-every-cross-plane-trip-must-leave-a-name" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: every cross-plane trip must leave a name&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Article 4&#39;s causal self-discipline has already established the principle; Article 14 lands it as a concrete administrative procedure: the reporting system. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s strong ones may traverse planes, but any cross-plane operation — regardless of purpose being diplomacy, rescue, archaeology, or cultivation — must in advance be reported to the Plane Administration Bureau, stating purpose, personnel, time limit, expected impact; no approval, no action. Reporting is not distrust of strong ones, but because cross-plane operations have an enormous causal-influence radius; one impulsive traversal may contaminate two planes.</p><p>This article is from beginning to end placed under the six top-level axioms — the anti-predation axiom draws the bottom line, the republican axiom of Myriad Races establishes the subject, the collective-ascension axiom sets the direction, the causal self-discipline axiom guards the boundary, the law-first axiom preserves self-consistency; the five together constitute this article&#39;s insurmountable spiritual boundary.</p><p>Together with the previous five axioms, this article is also bound by Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing and layabouts retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose more and higher levels of infinity; predation thus fundamentally loses meaning.</p><h2 id="i-jurisprudential-basis" tabindex="-1">I. Jurisprudential Basis <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-jurisprudential-basis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Jurisprudential Basis&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article is based on the Plane-Traversal Rules (Document 81), the Cross-Plane Ethics Guidelines (Document 88), and the Cross-Plane Anchor Connection (Document 28). Cross-plane operations directly touch the causal self-discipline axiom: only return knowledge, do not disturb causality. The reporting system turns this axiom from moral consciousness into administrative precondition — not &quot;do it then file afterward,&quot; but &quot;approved then allowed to move.&quot; Its jurisprudence is cognitive humility: even plane-sovereign strong ones cannot fully pre-judge traversal&#39;s full causal consequences; advance reporting is precisely to let professional institutions intervene in assessment.</p><h2 id="ii-normative-content-five-requirements-of-reporting" tabindex="-1">II. Normative Content: Five Requirements of Reporting <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-normative-content-five-requirements-of-reporting" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Normative Content: Five Requirements of Reporting&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Article 14 requires every cross-plane report to state:</p><ol><li><strong>Operation purpose</strong>: diplomacy, rescue, archaeology, cultivation, or cross-plane trade;</li><li><strong>Personnel list</strong>: who goes, each one&#39;s realm and authority;</li><li><strong>Time limit</strong>: estimated entry and departure time points;</li><li><strong>Expected impact</strong>: the disturbance range the target plane may suffer;</li><li><strong>Return method</strong>: the commitment to only return knowledge, no material energy.</li></ol><p>All five required for acceptance; after approval a cross-plane travel permit is issued.</p><h2 id="iii-scope" tabindex="-1">III. Scope <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-scope" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Scope&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article applies to all individuals and teams with cross-plane traversal ability, whether home-plane residents or external missions. Plane-sovereign strong ones and Multiverse Realm strong ones&#39; reporting review is stricter — because their causal-influence radius is larger. Traversing privately without a travel permit, regardless of reason, is uniformly unconstitutional. This article does not apply to emergency rescue: but rescue must immediately file a post-report and accept causal assessment.</p><h2 id="iv-consequences-of-violation" tabindex="-1">IV. Consequences of Violation <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-consequences-of-violation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Consequences of Violation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Traversing without approval, falsifying report information, overstaying beyond permitted purpose and time limit, using cross-plane channels to smuggle predated gains, all constitute unconstitutionality under this article. Consequences: forcibly withdraw, travel permit suspended; falsification and smuggling are pursued heavily under Article 1 anti-predation; those whose private traversal causes causal contamination, the operator bears all causal-correction costs and is permanently restricted from cross-plane qualification.</p><h2 id="v-supervision-mechanism" tabindex="-1">V. Supervision Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-supervision-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Supervision Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article is executed by the cross-plane travel ledger within Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision: every traversal&#39;s start, end, personnel, and time are fully traced, automatically compared with report records, mismatch immediately alerts; the Plane Administration Bureau sets up dedicated approval and inspection posts; the Time-Law Committee periodically audits reporting compliance, putting an end to &quot;secret passages.&quot;</p><h2 id="vi-an-approved-travel-pass" tabindex="-1">VI. An Approved Travel Pass <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-an-approved-travel-pass" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. An Approved Travel Pass&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Article 14 in reality is an approved travel pass. An archaeological team plans to go to an unfamiliar plane; in their report form they clearly write purpose, personnel, 72-hour observation period, commitment to only return knowledge; after submission it is quickly approved. This travel pass is not distrust, but a joint protection — protecting them from causing a causal accident due to momentary impulse, and protecting that unfamiliar plane from unauthorized entry. When cross-plane exploration becomes a rule-following, everyone-certificated daily routine, freedom need not come at the cost of adventure. The reporting system looks tedious, but actually makes every departure leave with peace of mind and return clean.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><p><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: advance assessment avoids catastrophic correction after cross-plane operations, zeroing out hidden costs</p></li><li><p><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: smuggling and plane colonization both need cross-plane channels; the reporting system places these channels under monitoring</p></li><li><p><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-type protagonists traverse freely with no one managing; Heng Yuan Zhou every traversal has a report, time limit, and inspection</p></li><li><p><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: reporting applies equally to Myriad-Rank missions and individuals, no exemption because of a large clan</p></li><li><p><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: the reporting system lets cross-plane exploration infinitely expand without losing control</p></li><li><p><strong>Universal equal infinity</strong>: every being inherently possesses basic infinite power; the easygoing layabouts retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose higher-level infinity; predation thus fundamentally loses meaning</p></li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The cross-plane operation reporting system is the reins Heng Yuan Zhou puts on free exploration. The reins are not to trap exploration, but to let exploration go on forever — the farther one goes, the more one must know where one came from, where one is going, and what one left behind.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/81-位面穿梭规则.html">Entry 81 · Plane-Traversal Rules</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/88-跨位面伦理准则.html">Entry 88 · Cross-Plane Ethics Guidelines</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/28-跨位面锚点连接.html">Entry 28 · Cross-Plane Anchor Connection</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/905_模块5-第四条-因果自律原则.html">Entry 905 · Article 4 Causal Self-Discipline Principle</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',26)])])}const m=a(r,[["render",o]]);export{d as __pageData,m as default};
